EXT. TRENCH LINE, RAIN-SOAKED FIELD - NIGHT

A sheet of rain. Barbed wire sags in the flare light. Mud sucks at every boot.

LIEUTENANT ARCHIBALD "ARCHIE" PENROSE (30s, helmet strap loose, flashlight taped) crouches with a map. SERGEANT BAPTISTE ONWUACHI (40s, thick forearms, helmet dented) checks his rifle. PRIVATE ELIAS FJELDSTAD-MORENO (19, trembling, bayonet fixed) hugs the trench wall.

PENROSE
Sergeant, status?

ONWUACHI
Half the men are asleep.

FJELDSTAD-MORENO
I'm not asleep.

ONWUACHI
Nobody said you were.

PENROSE
Elias, keep your head down.

FJELDSTAD-MORENO
Yes sir.

ONWUACHI
(to the trench)
Fix bayonets! On my word!

A whistle shrieks. Penrose and Onwuachi look up as one. Elias presses his forehead to the mud.

PENROSE
(muttering)
Dear God.

ONWUACHI
Now!

The whole trench erupts. Men climb out of the earth. Elias stays frozen until Onwuachi hauls him up by the collar and drags him into the dark.
